.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.\" Title
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TH OMCppOSUSimulation 1 "" "OpenModelica @OM_MANPAGE_VERSION@" "OpenModelica User Commands"
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
OMCppOSUSimulation \- simulate an OMSU or FMU 2.0 generated by the OpenModelica C++ runtime
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B OMCppOSUSimulation
.RI [ options ]
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B OMCppOSUSimulation
loads a model that
.B omc
compiled with the
.B omsicpp
simulation code target, an OpenModelica simulation unit (OMSU) or an FMU 2.0
for model exchange, and simulates it with the OpenModelica C++ simulation
runtime.
.PP
It is not usually run by hand:
.B omc
generates a script next to the compiled model that calls it with the model's
settings, and extra arguments given to that script are passed on.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH OPTIONS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.SS Model
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-omsu\-name " name"
The name of the OMSU or FMU.
.TP
.BI \-a ", " \-\-omsu\-path " path"
The directory holding the OMSU or FMU.
.TP
.BI \-i ", " \-\-init\-file " file"
The initialisation XML file of the OMSU or FMU.
.TP
.BI \-R ", " \-\-runtime\-library " path"
The directory of the C++ runtime libraries.
.TP
.BI \-M ", " \-\-modelica\-system\-library " path"
The directory of the compiled model.
.TP
.BI \-\-input\-path " path"
The directory of the input files, such as the initialisation XML file. The
default is the directory of the compiled model.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-path " path"
The directory the result file is written to. The default is the directory of
the compiled model.
.
.SS Simulation
.TP
.BI \-S ", " \-\-start\-time " time"
The start time. The default is 0.
.TP
.BI \-E ", " \-\-stop\-time " time"
The stop time. The default is 1.
.TP
.BI \-H ", " \-\-step\-size " step"
The step size. The default is 0.
.TP
.BI \-G ", " \-\-number\-of\-intervals " n"
The number of intervals of the equidistant output grid. The default is 500.
.TP
.BI \-T ", " \-\-tolerance " tolerance"
The solver tolerance. The default is 1e\-6.
.TP
.BI \-I ", " \-\-solver " method"
The integration method. The default is
.BR euler .
.TP
.BI \-L ", " \-\-lin\-solver " method"
The linear solver. The default is
.BR linearSolver .
.TP
.BI \-N ", " \-\-non\-lin\-solver " method"
The nonlinear solver. The default is
.BR kinsol .
.TP
.B \-\-nls\-continue
Continue the simulation when the nonlinear solver does not reach the requested
precision.
.TP
.BI \-A ", " \-\-alarm " seconds"
Stop the simulation after this many seconds. The default is 360.
.
.SS Results
.TP
.BI \-F ", " \-\-results\-file " file"
The name of the result file.
.TP
.BI \-P ", " \-\-output\-format " format"
The result file format:
.B mat
(the default),
.BR csv ,
.B buffer
or
.BR empty .
.TP
.BI \-O ", " \-\-output\-type " type"
The points in time written to the result file:
.B all
(output steps and events, the default),
.B step
(output steps only) or
.BR none .
.TP
.BI \-U ", " \-\-emit\-results " which"
The variables written to the result file:
.B public
(the default),
.B all
or
.BR none .
.
.SS Logging
.TP
.BI \-V ", " \-\-log\-settings " settings"
What to log:
.BR init ,
.BR nls ,
.BR ls ,
.BR solver ,
.BR output ,
.BR events ,
.B model
or
.BR other .
.TP
.BI \-X ", " \-\-log\-format " format"
The log format:
.B txt
(the default),
.B xml
or
.BR xmltcp .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-port " port"
The TCP port log messages are sent to. The default, 0, writes them to standard
output and standard error.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-warn\-all
Issue all warning messages.
.
.SS ZeroMQ
.TP
.BI \-u ", " \-\-use\-zeromq " bool"
Communicate with other applications over ZeroMQ during the simulation. Off by
default.
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-port\-publish " port"
The ZeroMQ publishing port. The default is 3203.
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-port\-subscribe " port"
The ZeroMQ subscribing port. The default is 3204.
.TP
.BI \-g ", " \-\-zeromq\-job\-id " id"
Identifies the translation and simulation of one model.
.TP
.BI \-v ", " \-\-zeromq\-server\-id " id"
Identifies the omc ZeroMQ application that receives the scripting API commands.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-zeromq\-client\-id " id"
Identifies the client application that uses the omc ZeroMQ application.
.
.SS Other
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.
